IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `iga-gambler`

-- Interactive Gambling Act 2001 (Cth), ss 4, 5, 8-8E, 10B, 15, 15AA, 15C, 15D, 69A and Part 7B (the National Self-exclusion
-- Register) -- worked cases from the seat of the gambler.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, an ACMA decision, the Register rules or any Ministerial determination (none was deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_interactive-gambling-act-2001_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA life of Jake (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake): at 39 he plays Lotto on Saturdays, goes
-- to the casino on paydays, then takes to betting apps (k080, 1 September 2045). On 8 May 2046 his sister Chloe looks for a
-- way to have him excluded, finds none in WA, and he registers on BetStop himself and self-excludes from the casino (k081).
-- The scenario gives no period, balances, bet types or support person; the 12 months, Chloe as support person, the 340
-- dollar balance and the AFL and racing bets are the encoder's. Fixtures not named for an event are invented for the case.

